## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

Each report is counted once, by its id (the export repeats some reports across pages), and filed under its tenant's cause, as the desk counts. The one-day moves stay filed under parser and also get their own row.

## How to tell them apart

- **parser**: day and month swap places (7 April arrives as 4 July). It comes from a day-first
  tenant through the app, email, or a booking-v2 form. The tenant's locale decides this, not
  the reporter's browser.
- **hint**: the same swap, but only through the **booking-v3** form of a day-first tenant. The
  form's hint asks for `MM/DD/YYYY`, so people type the month first, and the form reads it day
  first. The parser fix doesn't touch the hint. It ended when booking-v3 was retired.
- **shift**: the month stays and the day moves by one (Tuesday 12 May shows as Monday 11 May,
  and Lisbon and Toronto get different days for the same meeting). A swap can't do that. Look
  at time-zone and DST handling when invites are sent.

## Why they ended up together

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. All three
  problems arrive with the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Dates mixed up"), so all
  three merged into one ticket.
- Intake tags reports from the reporter's **browser** locale. The cause depends on the
  **tenant**: its locale and its booking form. The tags are wrong in both directions, so don't
  split by tag.

## For the desk

1. Treat parser and hint as done. A new month/day swap after 5 October is a regression, so
   give it a new ticket.
2. Send every one-day move to #3 and keep it open until time-zone handling is fixed.
3. Decision 0001 needs a replacement record. Decisions aren't edited after they're accepted.

